[00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760]   Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for standing by and welcome to the Ingersoll RAND first
[00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.580]   quarter 2020 earnings conference call.
[00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.040]   At this time, all participants are in a listening mode.
[00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.940]   After the speaker's presentation, there will be a question and answer session.
[00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.880]   To ask a question during the session, you will need to press star 1 on your telephone.
[00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.560]   We ask that you please limit yourself to one question and one follow-up.
[00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.100]   If you require any further assistance, please press star 0.
[00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.880]   I would now like to hand the conference over to your speaker today, Vic Kinney, head of
[00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:35.640]   investor relations.
[00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.740]   Thank you.
[00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:37.940]   Please go ahead.
[00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.900]   Thank you and welcome to the Ingersoll RAND 2020 first quarter earnings call.
[00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:47.580]   I'm Vic Kinney, Ingersoll RAND investor relations leader, and with me today are Vicente
[00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.340]   Renal, chief executive officer, and Emily Weaver, chief financial officer.
[00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:55.360]   Our earnings release was issued this morning in a supplemental presentation.
[00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:25.540]   For more details on this call, please refer to our annual report on form 10-K, filed with the security
[00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:29.480]   and exchange commission, and our current report on form 8-K, filed with the security and exchange
[00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:34.600]   commission on May 1st, 2020, which are available on our website at www.irco.com.
[00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.940]   Additional disclosure regarding forward-looking statements is included on slide 2 of the presentation.
[00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.640]   In addition, in today's remarks, we refer to certain non-GAAP financial measures.
[00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.880]   You can find a reconciliation of these measures to the most comparable measure calculated and
